     mu      si   cian\n                                            co\n\n        A     Note: -tion and -cian are pronounced\n    .. | B48  The  ending -ic also moves the stress to the syllable before it. Listen to these examples.\n              scientist            scientific\n              economy              economic\n              atom                 atomic\n              artist               artistic\n         A    Note: When  a syllable changes from unstressed to stressed, or stressed to unstressed, the vowel sound\n              often changes. For example the letter O in atom is pronounced /2/, but in atomic, it is pronounced\n              the A in atom is pronounced /z/, but in atomic it is /a/.\n         A     Note: The ending -a/ does not change the stress of the word (see A above), so, for example, the stress is\n              on the same syllable in these two words: economic economical.\n\n\n     cS                 Pronunciation in Use", "char_count": 2887, "mean_conf": 88.82, "word_count": 315, "words": [{"text": "example", "x0": 264, "y0": 426, "x1": 425, "y1": 472, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "below.", "x0": 441, "y0": 424, "x1": 562, "y1": 461, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "ful", "x0": 701, "y0": 568, "x1": 747, "y1": 602, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "ful", "x0": 702, "y0": 624, "x1": 747, "y1": 659, "conf": 90, "bold": true}, {"text": "|", "x0": 778, "y0": 619, "x1": 796, "y1": 670, "conf": 90, "bold": false}, {"text": "ness", "x0": 822, "y0": 633, "x1": 894, "y1": 658, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "a", "x0": 717, "y0": 691, "x1": 734, "y1": 716, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "ble", "x0": 832, "y0": 680, "x1": 883, "y1": 715, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "a", "x0": 717, "y0": 748, "x1": 734, "y1": 771, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "ble", "x0": 833, "y0": 737, "x1": 883, "y1": 770, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "Here", "x0": 267, "y0": 861, "x1": 360, "y1": 895, "conf": 96, "bold": fa